course: dictionary
lesson: 14893
title: Reconstitute: making it whole again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Long words can look scary, but you can break them into parts. In reconstitute, «re-» means again, and «constitute» means to make up or form. So to reconstitute something is to make it whole, or form it, again. «Mum added water to the powder to reconstitute the milk.» The milk started as dry powder, and the water brings it back to milk.
explain: Look for context clues. «The dried mushrooms soaked in water for ten minutes, and then they were ready to cook.» Soaking in water and getting ready to cook tells you the mushrooms became usable again. Test your guess by swapping in a simpler phrase, such as "put back into its original form", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word has a second meaning, used for groups and systems. «After the club split up, the members reconstituted the committee in a new way.» Here the committee was formed again, often differently. The clue is that something had broken up first, so the group is being rebuilt.
fact: The prefix «re-» at the start of a word often means "again".
fact: «Reconstitute» means to make dried food or powder into its original form again by adding water.
fact: «Reconstituted» juice is made from concentrate: a thick or dried form of juice has water added to it.
fact: «Reconstitute» can also be a formal word meaning to form a group, organisation or system again, often in a new way.
fact: To work out which meaning fits, ask: is water being added, or has something broken up and been rebuilt?
exercise: «To make the soup, Dad had to reconstitute the dried mushrooms by adding water.» What does reconstitute mean here? | *To make dried food usable again by adding water | To throw the mushrooms away | To buy fresh mushrooms from the shop | To cook them until they turn black
exercise: «Some juice labels say "from concentrate", which means the juice was reconstituted.» What does reconstituted mean? | *Made back into juice again by adding water | Sweetened with sugar | Frozen solid | Poured into a glass
exercise: «After the club split up, the members reconstituted the committee in a new way.» What does reconstituted mean here? | Closed for ever | *Formed again, often in a new way | Painted in bright colours | Argued about the rules
test: «The powdered milk was reconstituted with water and tasted fine.» Which word is the main clue that helps you understand reconstituted? | Powdered | Tasted | *Water | Fine
test: Which word means to form a group again after it has broken up? | *Reconstitute | Divide | Decorate | Dissolve
exam: A teacher says, «We will reconstitute the school council next term.» What does reconstitute most likely mean? | Have a party for the council | Write a letter about the council | *Form the council again, often in a new way | Close the council for ever
